==Russian==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|ru|orv|авосе}}, from {{affix|orv|а|t1=but|осе|t2=here|nocat=1}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ru-IPA|аво́сь}}
* {{audio|Ru-авось.ogg|Audio|lang=ru}}

===Adverb===
{{ru-adv|аво́сь}}

# {{lb|ru|colloquial}} [[perhaps]], [[maybe]], [[possibly]], may still, might yet {{qualifier|low certainty}}
#: {{uxi|ru|'''Аво́сь''' [[повезти|повезёт]].|We/I may yet succeed. (with low certainty)}}

===Noun===
{{ru-noun+|аво́сь|m}}

# blind trust in divine providence; blind faith in sheer luck; blind trust in sheer luck; counting on a miracle
#: {{ux|ru|[[надеясь|Наде́ясь]] [[на]] '''аво́сь''', [[я]] [[решить|реши́л]] [[вы́ехать]] [[на]] [[встречный|встре́чную]] [[полоса|по́лосу]], [[что́бы]] [[объе́хать]] [[пробка|про́бку]].|Counting on a '''miracle''', I decided to slip into the oncoming lane to get around the traffic jam.}}
# faith in serendipity; counting on pure luck
#: {{uxi|ru|[[ру́сский]] «аво́сь»|said about the [[alleged]] [[unconcern]] of Russians and their [[tendency]] to [[rely]] on [[luck]]}}
#: {{uxi|ru|на '''аво́сь'''|counting on pure luck}}
#: {{ux|ru|'''Аво́сь''' с небо́сем води́лись, да о́ба в я́му ввали́лись.|"Avos" and "[[небось|Nebos]]" hung out together and both fell into a hole. (one can't rely on luck alone)}}
#: {{ux|ru|От '''аво́ся''' добра́ не жди.|Don't expect anything good from "Avos". (one can't rely on luck alone)}}

